# Trusted ingress into central Flex
# caption: What it settles. The dialed number resolves the client before any IVR chooses a Service Unit. "Ingress" is the webhook on the client's own number, not a second number and not a bridge. Task attributes are routing context, never an authorization boundary. Unknown numbers go to restricted triage.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Caller as End Customer
    participant Edge as Client number in shared account
    participant Core as Platform ingress
    participant Flex as Central Flex runtime
    participant Assist as CIC Assist
    Caller->>Edge: Call client-specific number
    Edge->>Core: Verified source account and original DID
    Core->>Core: Resolve ownership and create Interaction
    Core-->>Edge: Scoped correlation token and config
    Edge->>Flex: Native same-account routing
    Flex->>Core: Verify token and resolve Service Unit
    Core-->>Flex: Canonical routing context
    Flex-->>Assist: Authorized task offer
    Assist->>Core: Fetch scoped context
    Assist->>Flex: Accept via certified SDK path
    Flex-->>Core: Account-scoped call and task events
  